FINDINGS:
1. [BLOCKER] docs/GRAMMAR.md:346 — REPORT.md:11 claims the `async_function` / `async_call` productions were "removed", but they are still present (`async_function`, `async_call`, plus `parallel_block` with `'wait'`/`'until' 'done'`), kept under a note — a claimed removal the tree does not contain, i.e. fake completion — fix: either remove the productions or correct the REPORT to "kept with Not-implemented note".
2. [MAJOR] SPEC.md:1068 — the network section still documents `set response to wait network.get(...)` / `wait network.post(...)` as working syntax while SPEC.md:966 says `wait` is an ordinary identifier and the form "is not part of the language" — direct self-contradiction the `spec_no_longer_promises_*` test never checks — fix: mark the network `wait` examples Not-implemented or remove the prefix.
3. [MAJOR] docs/GRAMMAR.md:509 — `object_literal = 'new' identifier ...` plus the GRAMMAR.md:580 and SPEC.md:628,647 examples (`set person to new Person`) still promise `new` as a keyword while the lexer freed `new` (SPEC.md:1117 lists it as an identifier) and the parser has no `New` arm, so `new Person` is now two identifiers and a parse error — the same reserved-but-unread class the phase claimed to eliminate — fix: mark object_literal Not-implemented or remove it.
4. [MAJOR] tests/keyword_reservation_test.rs:132 — the REACHABLE `return` row uses snippet `to answer()\n    give back 1\nend`, which contains no `return` at all, so the behavioural half cannot fail if the `Return` arm is deleted — fix: use a snippet containing `return`, e.g. a function body with `return 1`.
5. [MAJOR] src/parser.rs:1541 — `parse_object` (`Expected object name`), `parse_object` parent (line 1564), and `parse_test` (line 1701) were not routed through `expected_name`, so `object if` reports a bare message naming no word, contradicting the phase claim that rejections name the word — fix: route these three sites through `expected_name` like the other twelve.
6. [MAJOR] phases/phase-049/REPORT.md:120 — gate arithmetic is impossible: `1410 passed (was 1408 before this run's two added tests)` while REPORT.md:90 says the new file holds 13 tests, and the file list shows six test files touched (constant, for_range, linter, module_system, object_model, unless) while REPORT.md:13-14 discloses only one corpus set (mislisted) and only `unless_test.rs` — fix: re-run `cargo test --all-targets` and quote real output, and list all six test-file edits.
